---
title: "Validation Summary"
description: "Lists a form's invalid fields as links above the form when it is submitted."
tags: [forms, accessibility, javascript]
usage: |
  Add the `validated-form` class and `novalidate` to a `<form>`, and put a
  `<div class="validation-summary" tabindex="-1" hidden>` with a heading and an
  empty `<ul>` at the top. Then call `initValidationSummaries()`:

  ```js
  import { initValidationSummaries } from "./validation-summary.js";

  initValidationSummaries(); // or initValidationSummaries(root, ".validated-form")
  ```

  It uses the browser's constraint validation (`required`, `type`, `minlength`
  and so on) and its messages.
accessibility: |
  - On a failed submit, focus moves to the summary so the errors are read out.
  - Each error is a link that moves focus to its field.
  - Invalid fields get `aria-invalid="true"`, cleared on the next submit.
  - Every field needs a `<label for>`; its text is used in the summary.
customProperties:
  "--validation-summary-color": "Accent color."
  "--validation-summary-border-width": "Width of the accent border."
  "--validation-summary-background": "Background, mixed from the accent color."
  "--validation-summary-padding": "Inner spacing."
  "--validation-summary-margin-block-end": "Space below the summary."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<form class="validated-form" novalidate>
  <div class="validation-summary" tabindex="-1" hidden>
    <h3>Please fix the following</h3>
    <ul></ul>
  </div>
  <p>
    <label for="vs-email">Email</label>
    <input id="vs-email" type="email" name="email" required>
  </p>
  <p>
    <label for="vs-name">Name</label>
    <input id="vs-name" type="text" name="name" required minlength="2">
  </p>
  <button>Submit</button>
</form>

<script type="module">
  import { initValidationSummaries } from "./validation-summary.js";

  initValidationSummaries();
</script>
